# STM32 / CubeMX edit boundaries

## CubeMX owns peripherals

Peripheral configuration (SPI, GPIO, clocks, MSP) is **user-only via CubeMX**. See **`cubemx-configuration.mdc`**. Do not duplicate that setup in code.

## USER CODE blocks only

In CubeMX-generated files (`main.c`, `stm32u5xx_hal_msp.c`, `stm32u5xx_it.c`, `*_hal_conf.h` when it has blocks, etc.), **only** add or change code between:

```c
/* USER CODE BEGIN <tag> */
/* USER CODE END <tag> */
```

Never edit ST-provided code outside those markers — CubeMX regeneration will overwrite it.

Prefer new logic in:
- `USER CODE` sections for hooks tied to generated init (includes, `main` setup order)
- Separate project files under `Secure/Core/Src/` and `Secure/Core/Inc/` (e.g. `se_tropic.c`) for application modules

## Do not hand-edit generated build output

**Never edit anything under `Secure/Debug/` or `NonSecure/Debug/`.** CubeIDE regenerates these trees on every build (makefiles, `subdir.mk`, `objects.list`, `sources.mk`, `.o`, `.d`, `.elf`, `secure_nsclib.o`, etc.). Manual edits are lost immediately and waste review time.

### Forbidden paths (examples)

- `Secure/Debug/**`
- `NonSecure/Debug/**`
- `**/Debug/makefile`, `**/Debug/**/subdir.mk`, `**/Debug/objects.list`, `**/Debug/sources.mk`

### Where to make build changes instead

| Goal | Edit |
|------|------|
| Add/remove source files | `Secure/.project` linked resources + `Secure/.cproject` `sourceEntries` |
| Compiler defines / `-I` paths | `Secure/.cproject` (Debug + Release tool settings) |
| Include paths (NonSecure) | `NonSecure/.cproject` |
| Enable HAL IP | CubeMX `.ioc` → regenerate |
| Application logic | `Secure/Core/Src/`, `NonSecure/Core/Src/` |

After changing `.project` / `.cproject` or CubeMX, tell the user to **Build** in STM32CubeIDE so Debug output regenerates — do not patch Debug yourself.

- Enable HAL modules via **CubeMX `.ioc`**, not compiler `-D` overrides in `.cproject`

## External / vendored trees

- **`libtropic/`** — read-only; link via `.project` linked folders + `.cproject` includes/defines
- **`Middlewares/Third_Party/`** — do not patch; configure through project settings

## Examples

```c
// GOOD — main.c USER CODE 2 (after MX_GPIO_Init from CubeMX)
se_tropic_hw_init();

// BAD — editing MX_GPIO_Init body outside USER CODE
static void MX_GPIO_Init(void) {
  __HAL_RCC_GPIOB_CLK_ENABLE();  // lost on CubeMX regen
}

// BAD — manual HAL_SPI_MspInit anywhere (use CubeMX regen)
void HAL_SPI_MspInit(SPI_HandleTypeDef *hspi) { ... }

// BAD — editing Secure/Debug/Middlewares/libtropic/subdir.mk (lost on next build)
// GOOD — add libtropic linked folder in Secure/.project + includes in Secure/.cproject, then user rebuilds
```
